  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 258 PM EDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nPushing into Sunday, the threat for heavy rainfall and storms will\npush into east central Georgia as the low pressure system pushes\neastward and the front begins to push out of the area into\nsouthern Georgia, FL and the Carolinas. CAMs are beginning to be\nin range of this time frame and with the increased PWATs (2-2.2\")\ncontinuing and modest CAPE values there likely will be at least a\ncouple of strong to marginally severe storms. The main threats\nwill be locally damaging wind gusts and heavy rainfall that could\nlead to localized flooding. \n\nOnce the low pressure system pushes off into the Atlantic, the\narea will be in a more southwesterly flow pattern which will put\nus back into a more summer like pattern with daily afternoon \npopup thunderstorms each afternoon through the end of the week. \nTemperatures will be slower to warm up through the week by Friday \nhighs will be in the low to mid 90s.",
